  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the sources satisfy `requirements.ci.inputs`. The implementation covers every obligation, it is marked with `{impl}`, and tests cover the main cases.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `validate_file_range_input` (src/evidence.rs) checks the input's keys and parses `file`, `line_start`, `line_end` and `text`. It rejects an empty file name and non-positive line numbers. It reports `line_end must be at least line_start` when the range is out of order. It then calls `validate_input_lines`, and also calls `InputSelector::resolve` to produce the resolved input.\n- `validate_input_lines` (src/evidence.rs) reads the file through `read_project_file`. A missing or unreadable file is reported as an error, for example `cannot open missing.txt`. It splits the content into raw lines, stripping only a trailing `\\r`. It reports `exceeds the file's N lines` when `end` is beyond EOF. It reports a text-length mismatch against the range's line count. It reports `input text changed` with a compact diff when the lines differ from the recorded text.\n- `InputSelector::resolve` (src/inputs.rs) enforces the same range rules for the file-range form: `line_start` is at least 1, `line_end` is at least `line_start`, and `line_end` is within the file. `raw_lines` and `ResolvedInput` carry the `{impl}` marking for this requirement.\n- The helpers that implement other parts of the behaviour carry their own markings. These are `read_project_file` and `check_project_file` for `requirements.ci.input_containment`, `compact_diff` for `requirements.ci.diagnostics`, and the field parsers for `requirements.ci.schema`. I found no unmarked code implementing this requirement, and no behaviour beyond what it or another cited definition specifies.\n\n**Tests**\n- `file_ranges_report_order_eof_length_and_missing_file_errors` (tests/evidence_boundaries.rs) covers the valid range, an out-of-order range, a range past EOF, a text-length mismatch and a missing file.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` (src/evidence.rs) covers changed text with a diff, plus a zero `line_start`, an empty `file` and a non-string `text` entry.\n- `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` (src/evidence.rs) covers a valid range.\n- The boundary tests in tests/evidence_boundaries.rs cover symlinks, configured external inputs and Cargo output directories. They exercise freshness: a changed source produces `input text changed`. `fixme_does_not_hide_stale_inputs_or_uncovered_references` (tests/outcomes.rs) covers stale inputs showing up in the report.\n\n**Minor gaps, not enough to fail**\n- CRLF handling and an empty file are not tested explicitly.\n- Stripping a trailing `\\r` is a reasonable reading of \"raw lines\".",
